      "title": "Archimedean base change of the orthogonal sublattice, nilradical and center",
      "hypotheses": "An automorphic Hermitian datum of rank n ≥ 0 over a CM extension E/F with CM involution σ_E, Hermitian matrix J ∈ GL_n(E), and complex embeddings φ_v : E ↪ ℂ indexed by the real places v of F intertwining σ_E with complex conjugation; an adelic point x with full self-dual point lattice Λ_x ⊂ Eⁿ; and an 𝒪_E-submodule R ⊆ Eⁿ with E-span W = E·R and orthogonal intersection P = {y ∈ Λ_x : ∀ s ∈ R, ⟨s, y⟩_J = 0}.",
      "statement": "Writing span_v(M) = span_ℂ φ_v(M) ⊆ ℂⁿ at each real place v of F: (1) span_v(R) = span_ℂ φ_v(W) and span_v(Λ_x) = ℂⁿ; (2) span_v(P) coincides with the Hermitian orthogonal complement (span_v(R))^{⊥_{J_v}} in ℂⁿ; and (3) every rational matrix Y ∈ M_n(E) in the stabilizer nilradical of W (skew-Hermitian for J and mapping Eⁿ → W⊥ → W → 0) embeds diagonally as (φ_v(Y))_v into the real stabilizer nilradical of (span_v(R))_v, and every Y in the rational center (additionally vanishing on W⊥) embeds diagonally into the real center.",
      "definitions": [
        "orthogonal lattice intersection P = Λ_x ∩ R^{⊥_J}",
        "archimedean complex span span_v(M) = span_ℂ φ_v(M)",
        "dual linear-form span D ⊆ (Eⁿ)* and coannihilator projection π : Eⁿ → W⊥",
        "diagonal archimedean embedding of rational nilradical and central matrices"
